#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:4
msgid "conan.tools.intel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:7
msgid "IntelCC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:9
msgid ""
"This tool helps you to manage the Intel oneAPI `DPC++/C++ <https://software."
"intel.com/content/www/us/en/develop/documentation/oneapi-dpcpp-cpp-compiler-"
"dev-guide-and-reference/top.html>`_ and `Classic <https://software.intel.com/"
"content/www/us/en/develop/documentation/cpp-compiler-developer-guide-and-"
"reference/top.html>`_ ecosystem in Conan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:14
msgid "This generator is **experimental** and subject to breaking changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:18
msgid ""
"macOS is not supported for the Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ (icx/icpx or dpcpp) "
"compilers. For macOS or Xcode support, you'll have to use the Intel C++ "
"Classic Compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:22
msgid ""
"Remember, you need to have installed previously the `Intel oneAPI software "
"<https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/tools/oneapi/toolkits."
"html>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:25
msgid ""
"This generator creates a ``conanintelsetvars.sh|bat`` wrapping the Intel "
"script ``setvars.sh|bat`` that sets the Intel oneAPI environment variables "
"needed. That script is the first step to start using the Intel compilers "
"because it's setting some important variables in your local environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:29
msgid ""
"When your profile specifies ``compiler=intel-cc``, Conan automatically "
"invokes the ``IntelCC`` generator. You don't need to declare it explicitly "
"in your conanfile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:34
msgid ""
"If you explicitly set ``tools.intel:installation_path=\"\"`` configuration "
"(empty string), Conan will **not generate** the ``conanintelsetvars`` "
"script. In this case, you are expected to have already activated the Intel "
"oneAPI environment manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:40
msgid "At first, ensure you are using a *profile* like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:44
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"os=Linux\n"
"arch=x86_64\n"
"compiler=intel-cc\n"
"compiler.mode=icx\n"
"compiler.version=2026.0\n"
"compiler.libcxx=libstdc++\n"
"compiler.cppstd=gnu17\n"
"build_type=Release\n"
"\n"
"[conf]\n"
"tools.intel:installation_path=/opt/intel/oneapi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:59
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"os=Windows\n"
"arch=x86_64\n"
"compiler=intel-cc\n"
"compiler.mode=icx\n"
"compiler.version=2026.0\n"
"compiler.runtime=dynamic\n"
"compiler.cppstd=17\n"
"build_type=Release\n"
"\n"
"[conf]\n"
"tools.intel:installation_path=C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Intel\\oneAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:76
msgid "Compiler mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:78
msgid ""
"Conan selects the appropriate compiler executables based on the ``compiler."
"mode`` setting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:80
msgid ""
"**icx mode**: Uses ``icx``/``icpx`` on Linux, or ``icx-cl`` on Windows (for "
"MSVC compatibility)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:81
msgid "**dpcpp mode**: Uses ``icx``/``dpcpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:82
msgid "**classic mode**: Uses ``icc``/``icpc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:84
msgid ""
"You typically don't need to specify ``tools.build:compiler_executables`` in "
"your profile. If you do specify it, it will take precedence over the auto-"
"detected values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:91
msgid "SYCL support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:95
msgid ""
"The ``dpcpp`` compiler is **deprecated** by Intel. The recommended way to "
"compile SYCL code is to use ``icpx`` with the ``-fsycl`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:98
msgid ""
"To enable SYCL compilation, use the ``compiler.mode=icx`` setting and add "
"the ``-fsycl`` flag via the build configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:104
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"os=Linux\n"
"arch=x86_64\n"
"compiler=intel-cc\n"
"compiler.mode=icx\n"
"compiler.version=2026.0\n"
"compiler.libcxx=libstdc++\n"
"compiler.cppstd=gnu17\n"
"build_type=Release\n"
"\n"
"[conf]\n"
"tools.build:cxxflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.build:exelinkflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.build:sharedlinkflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.intel:installation_path=/opt/intel/oneapi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:122
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"os=Windows\n"
"arch=x86_64\n"
"compiler=intel-cc\n"
"compiler.mode=icx\n"
"compiler.version=2026.0\n"
"compiler.runtime=dynamic\n"
"compiler.cppstd=17\n"
"build_type=Release\n"
"\n"
"[conf]\n"
"tools.build:cxxflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.build:exelinkflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.build:sharedlinkflags=[\"-fsycl\"]\n"
"tools.intel:installation_path=C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Intel\\oneAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:142
msgid "Custom configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:144
msgid ""
"Apply different installation paths and command arguments simply by changing "
"the ``[conf]`` entries. For instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:146
msgid "intelprofile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:146
msgid ""
"[settings]\n"
"...\n"
"compiler=intel-cc\n"
"compiler.mode=icx\n"
"compiler.version=2026.0\n"
"compiler.libcxx=libstdc++\n"
"build_type=Release\n"
"\n"
"[conf]\n"
"tools.intel:installation_path=/opt/intel/oneapi\n"
"tools.intel:setvars_args=--config=\"full/path/to/your/config.txt\" --force"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:161
msgid ""
"Run again a :command:`conan install . -pr intelprofile`, then the "
"``conanintelsetvars.sh`` script (if we are using Linux OS) will contain "
"something like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:164
msgid "conanintelsetvars.sh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:164
msgid ""
". \"/opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh\" --config=\"full/path/to/your/config.txt\" "
"--force"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:170
msgid ""
"The ``IntelCC`` generator can also be fully instantiated in the conanfile "
"``generate()`` method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:172
msgid "*conanfile.py*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/tools/intel.rst:172
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.intel import IntelCC\n"
"\n"
"class App(ConanFile):\n"
"    settings = \"os\", \"arch\", \"compiler\", \"build_type\"\n"
"\n"
"    def generate(self):\n"
"        intelcc = IntelCC(self)\n"
"        intelcc.generate()"
msgstr ""

